  "Question": "\\[ \\frac{2^1+2^0+2^{-1}}{2^{-2}+2^{-3}+2^{-4}} \\] equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\)",
    "B": "\\(8\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\frac{31}{2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(24\\)",
    "E": "\\(512\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Use \\(2^0=1\\) and \\(2^{-k}=1/2^k\\) for positive integers \\(k\\). The resulting fractions have denominators dividing \\(16\\), so multiplying the numerator and denominator by \\(16\\) removes all the fractional terms without changing the quotient:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2^1+2^0+2^{-1}}{2^{-2}+2^{-3}+2^{-4}}\n&=\\frac{2+1+\\frac12}{\\frac14+\\frac18+\\frac1{16}}\\\\\n&=\\frac{32+16+8}{4+2+1}\\\\\n&=\\frac{56}{7}=8.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe denominator is positive, so the divisions are valid. The value is \\(8\\), choice B.",
